 is `targetMin + (value - sourceMin) / (sourceMax - sourceMin) * (targetMax - targetMin)`, with no clamping, so values outside the source range extrapolate.\n\nChoices I made without asking:\n- **Default values:** Value 0.5, Source 0 to 1, Target 0 to 100.\n- **Equal source bounds:** if Source Min equals Source Max, it throws an `ArgumentException`, which Betta shows as a component error. The alternative was returning NaN.\n- **Output name:** the plain return value doesn't carry a name, so the output pin will show Betta's default label rather than \"Result\". Naming it would need a named tuple like `(double Result)`, which I didn't change.\n\nThe project's post-build step copies `BenchPlugin.dll` into `%AppData%\\Grasshopper\\Libraries\\Betta\\`, so the build also updated that installed copy. I didn't test the component inside Grasshopper.","ttft_ms":1875,"type":"result","duration_ms":19121,"uuid":"23dd1341-e676-4abf-aea8-de50f5825cb1","ttft_stream_ms":1581,"time_to_request_ms":272,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":75,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":31,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":101,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":17,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":11,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":210,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":391,"time_to_request_major_faults":12168,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"skill_listing","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":47,"major_faults":992,"setup_ms":5,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":13,"ambient_wait_ms":7,"render_ms":2,"producers":43,"token_counts":0},"tool_schema_build_detail":{"betas_ms":0,"waits_ms":1,"placement_ms":0,"render_ms":16,"after_ms":0,"other_ms":0,"tools":15,"new_schemas":15},"messa